@startuml BPMN_Approval_Workflow
!theme plain

title Award Approval Workflow - Activity Diagram

|Owner|
start
:Submit the award\n(category, organisation, date set);
|System|
:Open a request at the start level\n(levels the submitter alone would review are passed over);
:Set the deadline of the level;

repeat
    |Reviewer|
    :Open the request from the queue;
    if (Claimed by a colleague?) then (yes)
        :Wait, or take over from a lower level;
    else (no)
        :Claim it, or decide directly\n(the decision claims it);
    endif
    note right
        One by one or in a batch (4.1.4).
        A missed deadline: the hourly job marks the
        request once per level and e-mails the next
        level with a reviewer (4.2.2).
        Nothing escalates on its own.
    end note
    switch (Decision?)
    case (Approve)
        |System|
        if (Level >= category minimum?) then (yes)
            :Request and award APPROVED;\nverification badge when documents were checked;
            :Mail the owner «approved»;
            stop
        else (no)
            :Request ESCALATED to the next level\nnot passed over, new deadline;
            :Mail the owner «passed on»;
        endif
    case (Escalate)
        |System|
        :Request ESCALATED to the next level\nnot passed over, new deadline\n(409 no-higher-level at the rector);
        :Mail the owner «passed on»;
    case (Return, comment)
        |System|
        :Request RETURNED, award DRAFT;
        :Mail the owner the comment;
        |Owner|
        :Correct the award and resubmit (4.1.3);
        |System|
        :Request SUBMITTED at the same level;
    case (Reject, comment)
        |System|
        :Request and award REJECTED\nwith the reason;
        :Mail the owner the reason;
        stop
    endswitch
repeat while (Request open?) is (yes)

stop

@enduml
